{"book":34,"chapter":2,"context":{"chapter":2,"title":"The Lions' Den Destroyed","summary":"In vivid, fast-moving poetry Nahum pictures attackers in red storming Nineveh, chariots racing through its streets, the palace collapsing, treasure looted, and the lions' den emptied.","background":"Nineveh lay on the Tigris River, with the smaller Khosr River running through the city. 'The gates of the rivers shall be opened' (v. 6) may refer to water defenses or floodgates; a later Greek historian claimed floods breached the walls, but how literally to read the verse is debated. Assyrian kings decorated their palaces with scenes of royal lion hunts and pictured themselves as lions.","customs":[{"term":"Red shields and scarlet","verses":"2:3","note":"Shields may have been covered in red-dyed leather or painted red, and soldiers dressed in scarlet, a terrifying sight."}],"watchFor":["The taunt 'Where is the dwelling of the lions?' (v. 11): the predator becomes prey.","'Behold, I am against thee, saith the LORD of hosts' (v. 13)."],"connections":["Zephaniah 2:13-15","Isaiah 10:5-12","Ezekiel 32:22-23"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["עָלָה","'alah","H5927","HVqp3ms","he has come up"],["מֵפִיץ","mefitz","H6327","HVhrmsa","[one who] scatters"],["עַל","'al-","H5921","HR","on"],["פָּנַיִךְ","panayikh","H6440","HNcmpc/Sp2fs","face your"],["נָצוֹר","natzor","H5341","HVqaa","guard"],["מְצֻרָה","metzurah","H4694","HNcfsa","[the] fortification"],["צַפֵּה","tzapeh-","H6822","HVpv2ms","watch"],["דֶרֶךְ","derekh","H1870","HNcbsa","[the] road"],["חַזֵּק","chazek","H2388","HVpv2ms","strengthen"],["מָתְנַיִם","matenayim","H4975","HNcmda","[the] loins"],["אַמֵּץ","'ametz","H553","HVpv2ms","make strong"],["כֹּחַ","koach","H3581","HNcmsa","strength"],["מְאֹד","me'od","H3966","HAcmsa","exceedingly"]],"x":[[29003009,29003011,9],[14025008,14025008,8],[24051020,24051023,6],[24051011,24051012,5],[24050023,24050023,4],[24046003,24046010,3]],"xn":6},"2":{"w":[["כִּי","ki","H3588","HTc","for"],["שָׁב","shav","H